0,Indo-European migrations - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-European_migrations,"The Indo-European migrations are hypothesized migrations of peoples who spoke Proto-Indo-European (PIE) and the derived Indo-European languages, which took place from around 4000 to 1000 BCE, potentially explaining how these related languages came to be spoken across a large area of Eurasia, spanning from the Indian subcontinent and Iranian ...",Kamar,Indo-European
1,Proto-Indo-European society - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Indo-European_society,"Proto-Indo-European society is the reconstructed culture of Proto-Indo-Europeans, the ancient speakers of the Proto-Indo-European language, ancestor of all modern Indo-European languages. Historical linguistics combined with archaeological and genetic evidence have provided the current basis for understanding the culture and its people.",Kamar,Indo-European
